C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:573: Rabbith belonged to Issachar’s inheritance in the fertile Jezreel region, though its exact site is unknown. Its inclusion among the boundary towns records God’s careful fulfillment of the land promised to Israel.
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:575: 1Ch 6:72 From the tribe of Issachar they were given Kedesh, Daberath,
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:577: Jos 17:11 Within Issachar and Asher, Manasseh was assigned Beth-shean,…
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:582: Kishion was later assigned to the Levites among Issachar’s towns (Joshua 21:28). Levites living within the tribal territories provided instruction in God’s law and kept worship and covenant faithfulness before the nation.
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:584: Jos 21:28-29 From the tribe of Issachar they were given Kishion,…
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:591: Ebez cannot be identified with certainty today, yet it was known to the original recipients of the allotment. Even lesser-known towns formed part of the inheritance God gave His people, showing that His provision extended throughout the land.
