C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:704: Asher’s Inheritance
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:706: Joshua 19:24
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:708: The fifth lot came out
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:709: Asher received its inheritance after Judah, Simeon, Zebulun, and Issachar. The casting of lots under Joshua’s leadership placed the division of Canaan under the Lord’s sovereign direction, ensuring that each tribe received the portion appointed for it.
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:711: Jos 18:10 And Joshua cast lots for them in the presence of the LORD…
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:713: Num 26:55-56 Indeed, the land must be divided by lot;…
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:715: Num 33:54 And you are to divide the land by lot according to your clans…
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:717: for the clans of the tribe of Asher:
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:718: Asher, descended from Jacob’s son by Zilpah, received fertile territory in the northern coastal region of Canaan. Its land included rich agricultural areas suited for olive production, in keeping with Jacob’s blessing that Asher would provide “royal delicacies” and Moses’ blessing concerning abundant oil. Yet Asher did not fully drive out the Canaanite inhabitants of several cities, a failure that later exposed the tribe to continued pagan influence and compromise.
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:720: Num 26:44-47 These were the descendants of Asher by their clans:…
