C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:729: Helkath stood within Asher’s allotted inheritance and was later assigned to the Gershonite Levites as a city for their service (Joshua 21:31). The distribution of such places showed that worship and instruction were to remain woven into the life of every tribe.
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:735: Deu 33:24-25 And concerning Asher he said: “May Asher be the most favored…
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:738: Hali, meaning “necklace” or “ornament,” belonged to the northern portion of Canaan assigned to Asher. Asher’s inheritance included fertile land and access to coastal routes, yet the tribe was called to possess its inheritance in faithful obedience to the Lord.
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:740: Jdg 1:31-32 Asher failed to drive out the inhabitants of Acco, Sidon,…
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:745: Beten, meaning “belly” or “womb,” was among the towns marking Asher’s territory. Its location is no longer certain, but its inclusion records the care with which the Lord established boundaries for His people and fulfilled His promise to give Israel the land.
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:747: Jdg 5:17 Gilead remained beyond the Jordan.…
