C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:939: Jos 14:2 Their inheritance was assigned by lot for the nine tribes…
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:942: The listed towns formed the settled communities within Asher’s tribal boundaries, providing places for families, agriculture, worship, and defense. Asher’s territory reached areas associated with Sidon and Tyre, though the tribe did not fully remove the Canaanite inhabitants from several coastal cities (Judges 1:31–32). Israel’s incomplete obedience allowed pagan populations to remain in the land, creating spiritual and political pressures in later generations. God had faithfully given Asher a rich inheritance, but the tribe’s lasting security  [...]
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:950: Naphtali’s Inheritance
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:952: Joshua 19:32
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:954: The sixth lot came out
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:955: The allotment of the land by lot took place before the LORD at Shiloh under the leadership of Joshua and Eleazar, showing that Israel’s inheritance was received from God rather than seized by tribal ambition. Though the lot was cast by human hands, its outcome rested in the Lord’s sovereign purpose.
C:\Obsidian\Hermes\scripture\raw_data\biblehub_study_joshua_19.txt:957: Jos 18:10 And Joshua cast lots for them in the presence of the LORD…
